(5892351, 855005, 7786, '<td valign="top">Stunning image! The details, clarity and vividness of this image is exceptional on top of a very interesting and well captured subject.</td>', 'Stunning image! The details, clarity and vividness of this image is exceptional on top of a very interesting and well captured subject.', '2010-03-06 08:56:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(5892368, 856951, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: This is a pretty image, particularly the coloration of the leaf and your subtle application of a vignette. The slightly tone mapped look works too.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: The bubbles, though a major contributing element of the image aren''t as pretty as the leaf and there is something about the bubbles that looks a little unclean (by association, not actually).<br/> <br/>Overall: A nicely composed image - well made.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: This is a pretty image, particularly the coloration of the leaf and your subtle application of a vignette. The slightly tone mapped look works too. Critical stuff: The bubbles, though a major contributing element of the image aren''t as pretty as the leaf and there is something about the bubbles that looks a little unclean (by association, not actually). Overall: A nicely composed image - well made.', '2010-03-06 09:49:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(5892372, 857084, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: Really interesting POV - makes me tip my head back just looking at it! I particularly like the sort-of-blurry-flowness of the main column. You really get a sense of how close to one another these things are.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: The toning - perhaps you were maintaining detail in the columns but the low contrast in the image makes it looks a little flat.<br/> <br/>Overall: A nicely seen image but for me the edit robs it of some needed drama.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: Really interesting POV - makes me tip my head back just looking at it! I particularly like the sort-of-blurry-flowness of the main column. You really get a sense of how close to one another these things are. Critical stuff: The toning - perhaps you were maintaining detail in the columns but the low contrast in the image makes it looks a little flat. Overall: A nicely seen image but for me the edit robs it of some needed drama.', '2010-03-06 09:53:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(5892381, 857554, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: This is really fabulous! This crossing parallels contribute immensely to the image and the mist around the pylon is really compelling. The sky is full of drama too and the high local contrast of the foreground complements this.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: Nothing at all<br/> <br/>Overall: Very effective image - very well made.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: This is really fabulous! This crossing parallels contribute immensely to the image and the mist around the pylon is really compelling. The sky is full of drama too and the high local contrast of the foreground complements this. Critical stuff: Nothing at all Overall: Very effective image - very well made.', '2010-03-06 09:58:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(5892382, 857228, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: Funny title but actually an image that stands on its own merits too. You have managed to convey the feeling of the space and your low POV works really well.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: Not much - I suppose, lens correction to correct for the perspective may have helped keep all your verticals vertical and the light is necessarily flat - as befits a gallery.<br/> <br/>Overall: I quite like it!</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: Funny title but actually an image that stands on its own merits too. You have managed to convey the feeling of the space and your low POV works really well. Critical stuff: Not much - I suppose, lens correction to correct for the perspective may have helped keep all your verticals vertical and the light is necessarily flat - as befits a gallery. Overall: I quite like it!', '2010-03-06 10:02:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(5892384, 851891, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: Great juxtaposition of the natural and the man-made. I really like the muted colour palette too. Also the sense of coldness is quite pronounced.<br/> <br/> <br/>Critical stuff: The binoculars look ever so slightly haloed and the blown highlight in the gap in the clouds is a little distracting, mainly because of its proximity to the gull.<br/> <br/>Overall: A very enjoyable image which manages to transport the viewer.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: Great juxtaposition of the natural and the man-made. I really like the muted colour palette too. Also the sense of coldness is quite pronounced.  Critical stuff: The binoculars look ever so slightly haloed and the blown highlight in the gap in the clouds is a little distracting, mainly because of its proximity to the gull. Overall: A very enjoyable image which manages to transport the viewer.', '2010-03-06 10:09:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(5892385, 857534, 14476, '<td valign="top">Nice interpretation of Baker Beach and the Gate!</td>', 'Nice interpretation of Baker Beach and the Gate!', '2010-03-06 10:12:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(5892386, 857497, 14476, '<td valign="top">Excellent way to see and show these ''ordinary'' objects!<br/>Very well done.</td>', 'Excellent way to see and show these ''ordinary'' objects!Very well done.', '2010-03-06 10:13:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(5892387, 857134, 98339, '<td valign="top">would like to see a bit more detail in the feathers, just a little soft in the focus</td>', 'would like to see a bit more detail in the feathers, just a little soft in the focus', '2010-03-06 10:13:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(5892388, 852634, 98339, '<td valign="top">nice capture, I like the deep shadows in this</td>', 'nice capture, I like the deep shadows in this', '2010-03-06 10:13:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(5892389, 855904, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m sure your getting hammered for the excess smoothing - I did for my ''Headwear'' entry. I can see why you''ve done it - to emphasise the eyes (which it does) but I think just sparing the tip of the nose often makes this more acceptable to viewers.<br/> <br/>I can''t argue with your execution of this approach but I suspect you''re not pulling the most potential out of your original image in terms of a score given by a DPC audience.</td>', 'I''m sure your getting hammered for the excess smoothing - I did for my ''Headwear'' entry. I can see why you''ve done it - to emphasise the eyes (which it does) but I think just sparing the tip of the nose often makes this more acceptable to viewers. I can''t argue with your execution of this approach but I suspect you''re not pulling the most potential out of your original image in terms of a score given by a DPC audience.', '2010-03-06 10:14:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(5892390, 857590, 98339, '<td valign="top">really nice colors and tones, well done</td>', 'really nice colors and tones, well done', '2010-03-06 10:14:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(5892391, 854606, 98339, '<td valign="top">that''s a cool wall mural.  excellent capture</td>', 'that''s a cool wall mural.  excellent capture', '2010-03-06 10:14:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(5892392, 855246, 98339, '<td valign="top">looks pretty steep and slippery.  Personally I would like to see a richer tone with this...</td>', 'looks pretty steep and slippery.  Personally I would like to see a richer tone with this...', '2010-03-06 10:15:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(5892393, 856873, 98339, '<td valign="top">very different...what is this exactly? nice clarity</td>', 'very different...what is this exactly? nice clarity', '2010-03-06 10:16:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(5892395, 853743, 98339, '<td valign="top">that a surprised look if I saw one...cute capture</td>', 'that a surprised look if I saw one...cute capture', '2010-03-06 10:18:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(5892396, 856656, 98339, '<td valign="top">good detail in the head and a really nice bokeh background</td>', 'good detail in the head and a really nice bokeh background', '2010-03-06 10:18:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(5892397, 856780, 98339, '<td valign="top">hmmm this is really pretty, nice color</td>', 'hmmm this is really pretty, nice color', '2010-03-06 10:19:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(5892398, 857534, 98339, '<td valign="top">such a stormy day...love the deep rich tone of this</td>', 'such a stormy day...love the deep rich tone of this', '2010-03-06 10:19:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(5892399, 857432, 98339, '<td valign="top">just a little soft in the focus IMO</td>', 'just a little soft in the focus IMO', '2010-03-06 10:20:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(5892400, 857199, 98339, '<td valign="top">don''t think I''d want to be anywhere near that...way to cold for me...personally I would prefer the bird in the light rather than the shadows...</td>', 'don''t think I''d want to be anywhere near that...way to cold for me...personally I would prefer the bird in the light rather than the shadows...', '2010-03-06 10:21:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(5892402, 853768, 98339, '<td valign="top">beautiful reflections, well done</td>', 'beautiful reflections, well done', '2010-03-06 10:22:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(5892403, 857526, 98339, '<td valign="top">IMO I think I would have cropped out part of her arm and hand...they don''t add to the picture and I want to see more of just her framed face</td>', 'IMO I think I would have cropped out part of her arm and hand...they don''t add to the picture and I want to see more of just her framed face', '2010-03-06 10:24:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(5892404, 853901, 98339, '<td valign="top">that''s funny, more like the gull is asking if their done with their food...hmmm I like how you made this B&amp;W  just a little ka-ka</td>', 'that''s funny, more like the gull is asking if their done with their food...hmmm I like how you made this B&W  just a little ka-ka', '2010-03-06 10:25:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(5892405, 854917, 98339, '<td valign="top">really like this...beautiful dog</td>', 'really like this...beautiful dog', '2010-03-06 10:25:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(5892406, 857486, 98339, '<td valign="top">are those glass bubbles or real bubbles?  I like the old feel of this</td>', 'are those glass bubbles or real bubbles?  I like the old feel of this', '2010-03-06 10:25:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(5892407, 856209, 98339, '<td valign="top">needs to be mud on those boots to be out from the field...lighting is good and so is your focus</td>', 'needs to be mud on those boots to be out from the field...lighting is good and so is your focus', '2010-03-06 10:26:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(5892427, 857506, 100393, '<td valign="top">I gave the adjacent frame to this a 7 in the ''shoes'' challenge so I do like the image but I''m not sure that it does so well in Free Study company - a lot of the appeal in the image comes from the idea and the smile that brings; I''m not sure it works as well as a second offering.</td>', 'I gave the adjacent frame to this a 7 in the ''shoes'' challenge so I do like the image but I''m not sure that it does so well in Free Study company - a lot of the appeal in the image comes from the idea and the smile that brings; I''m not sure it works as well as a second offering.', '2010-03-06 11:07:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(5892430, 852373, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: This one made me smile - I was going to say that it isn''t the sort of thing you''d put on your wall but actually I think it would look kinda good in the right place! I like the way the image offer an insight into a life - a nice idea. The border is cleverly matched too.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: Not too much - I''d perhaps take down the colour temperature a little.<br/> <br/>Overall: Good idea, pretty well executed too.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: This one made me smile - I was going to say that it isn''t the sort of thing you''d put on your wall but actually I think it would look kinda good in the right place! I like the way the image offer an insight into a life - a nice idea. The border is cleverly matched too. Critical stuff: Not too much - I''d perhaps take down the colour temperature a little. Overall: Good idea, pretty well executed too.', '2010-03-06 11:12:22.000000', NULL, 1);
INSERT INTO comments ("id", "image_id", "commenter_id", "raw_comment", "comment", "date", "edited", "made_during_challenge") VALUES
(5892432, 855582, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: There''s something about this image that make it standout - it actually pulled me make from the next one in voting . I think the slight tone mapping is measured to perfection and so is are the saturation levels too. The overall subject is pretty enough too but I get a real sense of your photography actually adding to the scene.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: Not much - perhaps you could have added some more contrast into the sky, though I admit that might detract attention away from your primary subject.<br/> <br/>Overall: A very well crafted image.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: There''s something about this image that make it standout - it actually pulled me make from the next one in voting . I think the slight tone mapping is measured to perfection and so is are the saturation levels too. The overall subject is pretty enough too but I get a real sense of your photography actually adding to the scene. Critical stuff: Not much - perhaps you could have added some more contrast into the sky, though I admit that might detract attention away from your primary subject. Overall: A very well crafted image.', '2010-03-06 11:16:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(5892437, 856386, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: What a beautifully composed image - very subtle indeed. It communicates a sense of silence and delicacy. I like the way that nothing has been ''pushed'' in the edit and as such the image feels honest.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: Nothing at all.<br/> <br/>Overall: Very nicely done</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: What a beautifully composed image - very subtle indeed. It communicates a sense of silence and delicacy. I like the way that nothing has been ''pushed'' in the edit and as such the image feels honest. Critical stuff: Nothing at all. Overall: Very nicely done', '2010-03-06 11:21:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(5892445, 855880, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: I really like this - I like the way that it doesn''t try to conform to normal portrait conventions - the folded limbs, the high contrast, the stern expression - more than the sum of the parts.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: Not much - I''d have perhaps smoothed the right forearm just proximal to the wrist band a little.<br/> <br/>Overall: Nice work.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: I really like this - I like the way that it doesn''t try to conform to normal portrait conventions - the folded limbs, the high contrast, the stern expression - more than the sum of the parts. Critical stuff: Not much - I''d have perhaps smoothed the right forearm just proximal to the wrist band a little. Overall: Nice work.', '2010-03-06 11:25:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(5892452, 854088, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: I like the way this is all about contrasts; contrasts of colour and texture and orientation and even in the way the eyes moves -into the picture with the red and upward with the green. You have made exactly the right choice with your DOF too.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: The limited number of elements might not appeal to everyone.<br/> <br/>Overall: Well seen and well executed.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: I like the way this is all about contrasts; contrasts of colour and texture and orientation and even in the way the eyes moves -into the picture with the red and upward with the green. You have made exactly the right choice with your DOF too. Critical stuff: The limited number of elements might not appeal to everyone. Overall: Well seen and well executed.', '2010-03-06 11:35:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(5892456, 853927, 59267, '<td valign="top">Beautiful!! Excellent lighting!</td>', 'Beautiful!! Excellent lighting!', '2010-03-06 11:44:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(5892460, 853582, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: This is certainly an unusual composition - inspired by the Children''s Toy / robot weirdness stuff going on? Whatever the motivation - it is very well done though. I think the DOF is just right too.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: It is what it is but I wonder if it runs a little short on overall interest level.<br/> <br/>Overall: I like it but I''m sure you knew that this was never going to garner wide appeal.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: This is certainly an unusual composition - inspired by the Children''s Toy / robot weirdness stuff going on? Whatever the motivation - it is very well done though. I think the DOF is just right too. Critical stuff: It is what it is but I wonder if it runs a little short on overall interest level. Overall: I like it but I''m sure you knew that this was never going to garner wide appeal.', '2010-03-06 12:04:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(5892465, 857557, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: I do like this and your title really helps to add interest - I''m sure I would not have twigged without the mental prompt. Stunning backdrop and an interesting foreground too. I feel that I''m getting a glimpse of the world that I''d never get without this photo - true of most images I suppose but this one seems to be particularly poignant in that regard.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: I suppose I wish it was slightly sharper.<br/> <br/>Overall: An image that has surprised me by how much it has caused me to reflect - that''s got to be a good thing hasn''t it?<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2010-03-10 11:43:44.</i></td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: I do like this and your title really helps to add interest - I''m sure I would not have twigged without the mental prompt. Stunning backdrop and an interesting foreground too. I feel that I''m getting a glimpse of the world that I''d never get without this photo - true of most images I suppose but this one seems to be particularly poignant in that regard. Critical stuff: I suppose I wish it was slightly sharper. Overall: An image that has surprised me by how much it has caused me to reflect - that''s got to be a good thing hasn''t it?', '2010-03-06 12:08:43.000000', '2010-03-10 11:43:44.000000', 1),
(5892467, 857675, 100393, '<td valign="top">My word - this has a 3D effect the like of which I''m not sure I''ve encountered before. Quite startling!</td>', 'My word - this has a 3D effect the like of which I''m not sure I''ve encountered before. Quite startling!', '2010-03-06 12:10:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(5892469, 856344, 49788, '<td valign="top">Wonderful portrait. Nice tones, good composition, and interesting lighting to isolate the face. Great sharpness in the eyes.</td>', 'Wonderful portrait. Nice tones, good composition, and interesting lighting to isolate the face. Great sharpness in the eyes.', '2010-03-06 12:12:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(5892471, 857269, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m sure this will hit all the the right buttons with a lot of people. A bit too ''fantasy art'' for my taste but the quality of the execution is amazing.</td>', 'I''m sure this will hit all the the right buttons with a lot of people. A bit too ''fantasy art'' for my taste but the quality of the execution is amazing.', '2010-03-06 12:15:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(5892475, 856679, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: Very interesting image - the style seems quite counter-wedding (though I appreciate that infers an expectation of cliche) - the POV and the billowing fabric is wonderful and the focus is right where it should be. I also like the way you have included quite a lot of the environment to set the context.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: nothing really.<br/> <br/>Overall: I like it!</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: Very interesting image - the style seems quite counter-wedding (though I appreciate that infers an expectation of cliche) - the POV and the billowing fabric is wonderful and the focus is right where it should be. I also like the way you have included quite a lot of the environment to set the context. Critical stuff: nothing really. Overall: I like it!', '2010-03-06 12:25:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(5892492, 857063, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: Very brave decision to go with this tint on a snow scene but for me it definitely adds. I think the placement of the elements is just about right.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: I don''t think there is that much interest in the scene to it tops out quite quickly for a viewer.<br/> <br/>Overall: I like the overall tones of the image but I''m not sure it is enough to truly carry the image.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: Very brave decision to go with this tint on a snow scene but for me it definitely adds. I think the placement of the elements is just about right. Critical stuff: I don''t think there is that much interest in the scene to it tops out quite quickly for a viewer. Overall: I like the overall tones of the image but I''m not sure it is enough to truly carry the image.', '2010-03-06 13:07:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(5892551, 857673, 46177, '<td valign="top">Very nice portrait!  Good luck.</td>', 'Very nice portrait!  Good luck.', '2010-03-06 15:08:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(5892555, 856227, 6179, '<td valign="top">Nice job on the dynamic range. This was a difficult capture. Looks like a Miles Morgan original. Love your work!</td>', 'Nice job on the dynamic range. This was a difficult capture. Looks like a Miles Morgan original. Love your work!', '2010-03-06 15:20:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(5892557, 857542, 83313, '<td valign="top">Nice nature shot. I assume you have to be patient for things like this to come along. I like what you did with the title. Does it seem to be effective in holding back critiques of "the subject does not stand out from the busy background"? (That''s what camouflage is <b>for</b>!!)</td>', 'Nice nature shot. I assume you have to be patient for things like this to come along. I like what you did with the title. Does it seem to be effective in holding back critiques of "the subject does not stand out from the busy background"? (That''s what camouflage is for!!)', '2010-03-06 15:41:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(5892558, 857198, 83313, '<td valign="top">All these very close up olympic shots I''ve been seeing in the challenges this week. You must have had a press pass, and maybe even known some of the right people.</td>', 'All these very close up olympic shots I''ve been seeing in the challenges this week. You must have had a press pass, and maybe even known some of the right people.', '2010-03-06 15:44:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(5892560, 855455, 83313, '<td valign="top">One of the more interesting duck shots I''ve seen in a challenge. In spite of all the busyness of the scene, my eye is drawn to the duck at the lower right third. Nice going.</td>', 'One of the more interesting duck shots I''ve seen in a challenge. In spite of all the busyness of the scene, my eye is drawn to the duck at the lower right third. Nice going.', '2010-03-06 15:47:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(5892562, 854356, 83313, '<td valign="top">I like what you did with this one. Haven''t gotten around to finishing up on  my own shots yet. Looks like we are both in the same range. Freestudies are certainly harsh. I''d figure this for an easy 6+ in any other challenge. (no vote, comment only)</td>', 'I like what you did with this one. Haven''t gotten around to finishing up on  my own shots yet. Looks like we are both in the same range. Freestudies are certainly harsh. I''d figure this for an easy 6+ in any other challenge. (no vote, comment only)', '2010-03-06 15:47:49.000000', NULL, 1),
