(5893902, 855892, 63218, '<td valign="top">For the combination of crisp edges &amp; interesting DOF &amp; lovely bokeh, &amp; great colors &amp; excellent camera angle &amp; absolutely no imperfection...the Gilded Lily is all I have to give, that &amp; HIP HIP HOORAY for you!<br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=831779" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/60000-64999/63218/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_831779.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/60000-64999/63218/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_831779.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/60000-64999/63218/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_831779.jpg"/></a></td>', 'For the combination of crisp edges & interesting DOF & lovely bokeh, & great colors & excellent camera angle & absolutely no imperfection...the Gilded Lily is all I have to give, that & HIP HIP HOORAY for you!', '2010-03-07 21:38:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(5893923, 857239, 63218, '<td valign="top">Stylin''! It might be my overactive imagination but this rose look as if some piece of mad scientists'' lab equipment has removed all its fragrance without touching it. Or a vampire rose--touch it &amp; watch it crumple to dust. "D It''s difficult to find an effective PP like this--applause to you for doing it, &amp; here''s my Guilded Lily for your magical PP. It would look good on a label for a perfume.<br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=831779" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/60000-64999/63218/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_831779.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/60000-64999/63218/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_831779.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/60000-64999/63218/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_831779.jpg"/></a></td>', 'Stylin''! It might be my overactive imagination but this rose look as if some piece of mad scientists'' lab equipment has removed all its fragrance without touching it. Or a vampire rose--touch it & watch it crumple to dust. "D It''s difficult to find an effective PP like this--applause to you for doing it, & here''s my Guilded Lily for your magical PP. It would look good on a label for a perfume.', '2010-03-07 21:58:21.000000', NULL, 1),
