(5902929, 857554, 106543, '<td valign="top"><b>Greetings from the Critique Club! </b> <br/> <br/>Is it the water in Iceland? It seems that every photo from an Icelandic photographer is beautiful, it''s just not fair :). This was one of my highest rated images in the free study. You received a solid score and getting in the top 20 is awesome!  I love the snow drifting in the field and the range of light throughout the entire picture.<br/> <br/>In regard to the negatives of this image, there are none. It would take a much more skilled photographer than me to give you any advice. In fact I shouldn''t even be allowed to critique this haha. Overall it''s a great image with great black and white processing, and I really hope to see you enter more challenges!<br/> <br/>If you have any questions <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/messaging.php?action=compose&amp;USER_ID=106543" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">click here to message me</a>! <br/> <br/>Senay</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club!   Is it the water in Iceland? It seems that every photo from an Icelandic photographer is beautiful, it''s just not fair :). This was one of my highest rated images in the free study. You received a solid score and getting in the top 20 is awesome!  I love the snow drifting in the field and the range of light throughout the entire picture. In regard to the negatives of this image, there are none. It would take a much more skilled photographer than me to give you any advice. In fact I shouldn''t even be allowed to critique this haha. Overall it''s a great image with great black and white processing, and I really hope to see you enter more challenges! If you have any questions click here to message me!  Senay', '2010-03-13 20:01:49.000000', NULL, 0),
