(5903733, 857382, 106543, '<td valign="top"><b>Greetings from the Critique Club! </b> <br/> <br/>Ouch, last place!?? I think that''s a little bit harsh. You received some helpful comments during voting and I have to agree with them. It may be out of focus or just soft. That combined with the far away bird that is facing away from the viewer really seemed to hurt you with the voters. One thing that I don''t really know what it is but it detracts from your image is the black dots that are everywhere except for the sky and the white on the bird. I guess it''s not noise since you only used ISO 400. It might be due to the cropping but I really have no idea :S. Congratulations on the brown ribbon and good luck on your future challenge entries!<br/> <br/>If you have any questions <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/messaging.php?action=compose&amp;USER_ID=106543" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">click here to message me</a>! <br/> <br/>Senay</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club!   Ouch, last place!?? I think that''s a little bit harsh. You received some helpful comments during voting and I have to agree with them. It may be out of focus or just soft. That combined with the far away bird that is facing away from the viewer really seemed to hurt you with the voters. One thing that I don''t really know what it is but it detracts from your image is the black dots that are everywhere except for the sky and the white on the bird. I guess it''s not noise since you only used ISO 400. It might be due to the cropping but I really have no idea :S. Congratulations on the brown ribbon and good luck on your future challenge entries! If you have any questions click here to message me!  Senay', '2010-03-14 13:18:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(5903937, 857672, 18799, '<td valign="top">Hi, Critique Club here...<br/> <br/>I think this is a really fun image and one that will take it''s place well in the family album.  I love the glasses.<br/> <br/>I think there are a few problems that resulted in the lower score.<br/>1) It has a very snap shot type feel to it.  Not that there is anything wrong with that, but for a free study, it won''t do well right out of the shoot.<br/>2) There is a fair about noise in the image.  <br/>3) Her face is a bit dirty (sand or something)<br/>4) The strong lines in the background are not good (for a higher score that is)<br/>5) Her expression is rather odd.  Once again, ok for a snapshot, not for a free study.<br/> <br/>The devil is always in the details for these challenges.<br/> <br/>Just one person''s opinions so take it with a grain of salt.</td>', 'Hi, Critique Club here... I think this is a really fun image and one that will take it''s place well in the family album.  I love the glasses. I think there are a few problems that resulted in the lower score.1) It has a very snap shot type feel to it.  Not that there is anything wrong with that, but for a free study, it won''t do well right out of the shoot.2) There is a fair about noise in the image.  3) Her face is a bit dirty (sand or something)4) The strong lines in the background are not good (for a higher score that is)5) Her expression is rather odd.  Once again, ok for a snapshot, not for a free study. The devil is always in the details for these challenges. Just one person''s opinions so take it with a grain of salt.', '2010-03-14 15:48:07.000000', NULL, 0),
